  "default_and_exp3_archive_parity": true,
  "decision": "Keep disabled by default. Averaging improves several Exp3 comparisons and avoids the known bad mixture, but ordinary-budget fresh-policy losses remain worse than UCB on both sides. The cumulative gated P0 mixture improves slightly; P1 retains the same pure fallback. These mixed signals do not establish general strength or justify adoption.",
  "scope": "Four paired search seeds at 27000 simulations with fixed fresh probes, plus the known adaptive-probe counterexample at 108000 simulations. Both players are tested on legally replayed known-team Bond states. UCB and pre-existing Exp3 controls reproduce archived search rows exactly. Only non-root, non-preview Exp3 updates use sampled successor-decision mean returns; raw terminal returns still feed every node, public action totals and the root matrix. Forced nodes and newly expanded leaves receive raw statistics. Terminal and horizon returns are not averaged, and no convergence theorem is asserted for this game. Losses certify first-action distributions with optimal subsequent full-state play. Timing is diagnostic, not a matched-time strength result; the first UCB run overlapped the regression checks. The experimental flag is off by default."
}
